speechtext:
I think this discussion-would be more appropriate on the substituted clauses prescribing the methods by which this enumeration s-ha-ll be made. However, as the subject is up, I know that the hon. member for St. John has made one important omission in his speech. He does not say before what tribunal, or by what machinery, -these additional voters are to be put on the lists in his or any other province. It must be remembered that these votes are scattered over the length and;

breadth of very large constituencies. The constituency of Halifax in Nova Scotia, for instance, is over seventy-five miles long.
Mr. PU'GSLEY: Mine is twice as long as that.
